%N A401876 Number of induced cubes in the Kneser graph KG(n,2).
%C A401876 The dimension of an induced cube in the Kneser KG(n,2) graph is at most 3. The induced cube polynomial is binomial(n,2) + 3*binomial(n,4)*x + 90*binomial(n,6)*x^2 + 15*binomial(n,6)*x^3.
%C A401876 All 3-dimensional cubes up to relabeling are of the form:
%C A401876     12------45
%C A401876      | \     | \
%C A401876      |   34--|--16
%C A401876      |   |   |   |
%C A401876     46------13   |
%C A401876       \  |     \ |
%C A401876         15------24
%C A401876 In the above, the labels are pairs of integers in the range 1..n, a vertex is adjacent if and only there is no common integer in their labels.
%C A401876 The above diagram can be written in tabular form:
%C A401876   000  001  010  011  100  101  110  111
%C A401876   (12) (45) (46) (13) (34) (16) (15) (24)
%H A401876 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A401876/b401876.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1000</a>
%H A401876 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/CubePolynomial.html">Cube Polynomial</a>.
%H A401876 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/KneserGraph.html">Kneser Graph</a>.
%H A401876 <a href="/index/Rec#order_07">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (7,-21,35,-35,21,-7,1).
%F A401876 a(n) = binomial(n,2) + 3*binomial(n,4) + 105*binomial(n,6).
%F A401876 a(n) = (7*n^6 - 105*n^5 + 601*n^4 - 1611*n^3 + 2008*n^2 - 900*n)/48.
%F A401876 G.f.: x^2*(1 - 4*x + 9*x^2 - 10*x^3 + 109*x^4)/(1 - x)^7.
%t A401876 A401876[n_] := {1, 3, 105}.Binomial[n, {2, 4, 6}]; Array[A401876, 35] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 21 2026 *)
%t A401876 (* Alternative: *)
%t A401876 LinearRecurrence[{7, -21, 35, -35, 21, -7, 1}, {0, 1, 3, 9, 25, 165, 861}, 35] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 21 2026 *)
%o A401876 (PARI) a(n) = binomial(n,2) + 3*binomial(n,4) + 105*binomial(n,6)
%Y A401876 Cf. A161680 (number of vertices), A050534 (edges), A065949 (squares).
